-TeamID: ataupd2425-gainer

-TaskID: 6.2.2

-RunID: TD1

-Training applied:
1) I split samples into train_test split an 80/20 train/validation set.

2) I fine-tuned a BertForSequenceClassification (in this case i used the NeuML/pubmedbert-base-embeddings) for 5 epochs, using a batch size of 8 and a learning rate of 2e-5 under an AdamW optimizer.

3) A linear warm-up schedule (no warm-up steps here) adjusts the learning rate over total_steps = epochs × steps_per_epoch.

4) During each training step I compute: cross-entropy loss, backpropagate, clip gradients, update both optimizer and scheduler.

5) Once training completes, I save the fine-tuned model.

-Pre-processing applied: 
1) First I load each article’s JSON entry: extracting its title, abstract, entities, and relations.

2) The entities are split into “title” and “abstract” , I keep the offset of the abstract ones.

3) For every positive relation (subject–predicate–object pair) entirely in the title or entirely in the abstract, I insert special markers [E1][/E1] around the subject span and [E2][/E2] around the object span in the raw text.

4) I added the negative samples and the negative ratio, in this case 0.3.

5) The marked sentences become the samples of the training dataset; during this phase I build a dictionary to keep the relations and the no_relation label and mapping them to a number (ex 1: interact).

6) Apply the tokenizer to each marked sentence with a BERT tokenizer, padding or truncating to 356 tokens.

-Training data: train_platinum.json, train_gold.json and dev.json

-Relevant details:

The negative ratio helped the model to discover the valid samples from the non valid one. The entity markers helped the model to map and learn the relations between entities.
The NER entities that are in the TEST dataset come from the ataupd2425-gainer_T61_ma_trainplatinumgolddev MODEL.

